A||||2||SCCA FIERO||Replacing oilpan gasket
Z||000000||SCCA FIERO||08-09-99||09:25 PM||||I need to repalce it to fix a leak. I would like to put in a high volume unit. How much do they cost and does anyone have one? What else should be done while it's off?
Z||000001||PaUL||08-10-99||08:23 PM||||I would say you should also change the rear main oil seal but, (I may be wrong on this) I think all fiero v6s came with the one piece seal and you need to remove the whole engine to change it. Earlier 2.8 v6 in other cars came with a 2 piece seal that could be changed from underneath with the oilpan removed.  
Z||000002||Speadraser||08-10-99||11:12 PM||||I just replaced my pan gasket about six months ago.  Its not hard and easily done on a lift.  You just have to loosen and/or disconnect one of the rear tailpipe hangers and the pan slides out quite nicely.  I wish I would have replaced my pump with a high-volume unit then, now I spun a bearing and am going to rebuild the whole thing.  Now's my chance to drop in a 3.1 crank and pistons.  I guess all things aren't bad but they seem to have some sh**ty timing!  Good luck!<br>Speady
